00:53:37.247 --> 00:53:39.883
Bretton Woods
 established an arrangement whereby

00:53:40.417 --> 00:53:43.720
supposedly from 1945
 and the end of the war onward,

00:53:44.688 --> 00:53:49.259
all currencies were convertible to the dollar
 and the dollar to gold.

00:53:49.426 --> 00:53:54.698
At that time gold reserves were
 the final mechanism for settling

00:53:55.031 --> 00:53:58.868
balance of payments deficits, but
 Bretton Woods forestall this process

00:53:59.135 --> 00:54:04.307
by permitting the sole reserve
 currency, the main reserve currency,

00:54:04.541 --> 00:54:11.481
to be considered as official reserves
 for foreign central banks.

00:54:11.481 --> 00:54:16.720
Such that they could settle all their
 deficits in dollars as opposed to gold.

00:54:16.886 --> 00:54:20.423
That's the fundamental difference
 between the classical gold standard

00:54:20.423 --> 00:54:23.426
and what is called
 the gold exchange standard,

00:54:23.660 --> 00:54:26.997
which Bretton Woods
 enshrined in law and in treaty.

00:54:27.030 --> 00:54:32.235
In 1971, both Britain and several
 other countries decided to in-cash

00:54:32.736 --> 00:54:38.341
